    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d558">

                <pb facs="0480" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg364"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.51/369.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Blanchard.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-04T11:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your December 2, 10 a.m. You may inform Theodore that an issue of paper money at
                    this time might compel the Department to cancel its offer contained in first
                    paragraph of its November 28, 8 p.m. Continue to keep Department fully
                    advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
